(import :clan/poo/object)
(export DesignReadings)
(def DesignReadings (.o inspections: (list (.o identity: 'reading-2fedbb95569a view: 'durable-owner-recovery revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-17425ce60d56b1e9f4ecca31df04ec9b19e8b2361240d16129ed5346aab9283b image-sha: "2fedbb95569af0df58b00e3e259585f0502cf72759feecc90db8c62310e03250" question: 'what-survives-an-owner producer: 'current-model response: "I viewed the final English PNG. The joined Context Feature and Durable shapes show module assembly. The middle card distinguishes evidence for this effect from the two retry checks. The right card retains the original Attempt with a matching binding and unknown effect. Its caption explicitly separates the actual positive policy proposal from the ineligible result. This matches the emitted DOC 19 decision. The arrows explain dependencies and may be read as a sequence without the accompanying text. Current authority and receipt consumption belong to the host contract in DOC 18 and are outside the visible decision card. The diagram is readable at the exported size. This feedback is about the rendered image.\n")
 (.o identity: 'reading-01e630c20dd3 view: 'durable-owner-recovery revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-8672919a1901de603c09ed771e3ad22b13803a2660dfcfab7365cfea4e1b675e image-sha: "01e630c20dd35acbbec702adc4e00c7f583b884eac14d1d5c3ab78f13deef712" question: 'what-survives-an-owner producer: 'current-model response: "I viewed the new PNG. The middle card splits the two policy inputs with a divider. Evidence for this effect sits under Outcome interpreter. Current permission and Safe to repeat? sit under Retry policy. The same Attempt shows a matching binding, an unknown effect and a held retry, so a reader can see why binding alone does not open the gate. The caption A retry still needs both checks reinforces the two independent guards. The image leaves admission of evidence and examples of safe repetition to the linked design. The arrows can still read as a sequence, although the source model declares dependencies and permits independent evidence arrival. This is a reading of the exported image, not a runtime or learner result.\n")
 (.o identity: 'reading-ae6a8a00f0f0 view: 'durable-owner-recovery revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-0421a9972237667b98293bea198c0a0f7b579f6df730ef6247ad88911e72a7d3 image-sha: "ae6a8a00f0f0a23d5099526f825918b42bd5dc14219af3a52a469fec23b39081" question: 'what-survives-an-owner producer: 'current-model response: "I viewed the exported PNG. The Context Feature and independent Durable provider are visibly joined at the Core contract seam. The middle configuration card names the outcome interpreter and retry policy as two Durable slots. The same Attempt ticket shows that a matching binding can coexist with an unknown effect and a held retry. The three columns read as dependency and use relationships, although the arrows can suggest a sequence to a beginner. The policy names alone do not show their distinct inputs. The next explanatory view should show that the outcome interpreter consumes effect evidence, while retry needs current permission and repeat safety. The right ticket remains open in this scenario.\n")
 (.o identity: 'reading-0ffd914038ba view: 'durable-owner-recovery revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-3502afed58e734b1b0b02698a2736b4c60eecfd8215d68436e5a7d796f567a41 image-sha: "0ffd914038bab1783c049abf3ef16c34884fb836afe1d3750895be29d23c9d84" question: 'what-survives-an-owner producer: 'current-model response: "I viewed the exported PNG. A single retained Attempt ticket branches to three peer questions. The two matching binding cards support reading the checkpoint. The empty effect receipt keeps the outcome unknown. The closed retry gate and its Permission + safe repeat label explain why the Attempt stays open in this case. I can trace any branch independently, including retry first. The layout leaves broad side margins and places retry at the top, but the common ticket and separate routes keep the illustration from implying a mandatory order. The receipt metaphor could lead a beginner to ask whether another trusted observation could count. The source admits other outcome evidence tied to the same effect identity. No runtime outcome is inferred from the picture.\n")
 (.o identity: 'reading-700ca4e9402e view: 'durable-owner-recovery revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-c6b05638d98da9490f88341fc789b6fbb59d15b444e6af7385839b52561aeecf image-sha: "700ca4e9402e496387788a92b3e26d358c1ba775c8db77edd6b59b5af59025d7" question: 'what-survives-an-owner producer: 'current-model response: "I viewed the second PNG. The journal is now the central clue: its saved decision remains, the original Attempt is unfinished, and the READY it holds names the previous owner. The new owner has a separate READY and its attached note explains reconstruction before readiness. The three objects are legible without zooming the way the four-column image required. The bottom route still takes two turns around the retained journal; it separates owner replacement from journal reconstruction, but costs a longer eye movement. The distinction between receiving new work and finishing the old Attempt is visible. A novice may still need the word Attempt explained as one try at doing the work. This is a model reading of this image, with learner response still unobserved.\n")
 (.o identity: 'reading-238ab01c81db view: 'durable-owner-recovery revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-c6b05638d98da9490f88341fc789b6fbb59d15b444e6af7385839b52561aeecf image-sha: "238ab01c81db1461ea34ccc3749513e0949fa53793356befe14e01adc8fe4d6b" question: 'what-survives-an-owner producer: 'current-model response: "I viewed the first recovery PNG. The old owner changes to a new owner while the saved journal retains a decision, an unfinished Attempt and historical readiness. The new owner rebuilds before its own READY, and its ability to receive work does not finish the old Attempt. These causal distinctions are present, but four horizontal illustrated columns shrink the reader text to about 15 pixels. ASCENT's existing 18-pixel reader threshold already exposes the failure. A new reader would have to decipher small labels and follow a long bypass around the journal. Rebuilding and becoming READY are explanations of the same new owner, not independent objects requiring two large illustrations. Preserve the rebuilding reason and all four facet obligations, but attach that reason to the new owner through its semantic referent rather than allocate a fourth canvas column. Do not widen a case-specific canvas, lower the text gate, delete the reason, or claim that a blank request list establishes comprehension. The old READY is historical; one local writer does not prove an external worker terminated.\n")
